    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but some of the senior devs are pushing back. They're arguing that if we force equal outcomes, we're effectively penalizing high-performing individuals and ignoring actual creditworthiness, which could make the model less accurate or even discriminatory against them. How would you respond to the argument that 'equality of opportunity' is a more mathematically sound and fair way to build a model?",
